<concept id="eco-rhwa-rel-notes-mapping-table">
  <title>Mapping the Workload Availability for Red Hat OpenShift release to the Operator releases</title>
  <conbody>
    <p>With some RHWA releases, the version numbers are based on the year and the iteration in that year. For example, 26.1 is the first release in 2026.</p>
    <p>However, some RHWA releases now also align with the latest release of Red Hat OpenShift.</p>
    <p>To distinguish between the Red Hat OpenShift release and the RHWA release, a <b>-Iteration</b>, is appended at the end of the RHWA release number.</p>
    <p>The latest release of Red Hat OpenShift is 4.21. Accordingly, the first, and latest release of Workload Availability for Red Hat OpenShift is 4.21-0.</p>
    <p>The Operator version numbers follow semantic versioning.</p>
